---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { getRelativeLocaleUrl } from 'astro:i18n';
const directoryUrl = getRelativeLocaleUrl('en', '/plugins/directory/');
---
<Base title="DeepSeek Harness Themes — 151 Skins &amp; Theme Center | dshbase" description="DeepSeek Harness theme center: dsh-themes with 151 day/night skin pairs, built-in palettes, Open VSX import, and a color editor. Install with dsh plugin add dsh-themes." currentPath="/themes/">
  <section class="hero wrap">
    <p class="eyebrow">Theme center</p>
    <h1>DeepSeek Harness <span class="accent">themes</span></h1>
    <p class="lede">Give your DSH Web UI a new look — <strong>151 day/night skin pairs</strong>, one install, one-click try-on.</p>
  </section>

  <section class="info wrap">
    <h2>Install</h2>
    <pre class="code-block"><code>dsh plugin add dsh-themes</code></pre>
    <p>Restart <code>dsh web</code>, then find the theme center in Settings → Plugins.</p>

    <h2 style="margin-top:28px">What you get</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>151 day/night skin pairs</strong> — grid preview, search, one-click try-on inside the DSH Web UI</li>
      <li><strong>Built-in palettes</strong> — curated color palettes ready to apply</li>
      <li><strong>Open VSX search import</strong> — import themes from the Open VSX marketplace</li>
      <li><strong>Color editor</strong> — tweak colors per-theme, with independent light/dark settings</li>
    </ul>

    <h2 style="margin-top:28px">About the theme system</h2>
    <p>DSH's appearance is plugin-driven — themes are just another plugin. <code>dsh-themes</code> bundles 151 pairs of skins (a day and a night variant each) so you can switch the whole UI in one click. It's part of the broader dsh-suite ecosystem and is MIT-licensed.</p>
    <p>See the full plugin entry for version, install status, and test result in the <a href="/plugins/dsh-themes/">plugin directory</a>.</p>

    <p style="margin-top:24px"><a class="btn btn-ghost" href={directoryUrl}>Browse all plugins &rarr;</a></p>
  </section>
</Base>
